{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,9]],"date-time":"2026-10-09T07:49:55Z","timestamp":1791532195232,"version":"4.3.4"},"reference-count":24,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"6","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,9]],"date-time":"2026-10-09T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1791504000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,9]],"date-time":"2026-10-09T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1791504000000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/doi.wiley.com\/10.1002\/tdm_license_1.1"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001659","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["GPF 21\u20101\/062"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["GPF 21\u20101\/062"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001659","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100003453","name":"Natural Science Foundation of Guangdong Province","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["2026A1515010276; the 2026 Foreign Experts Program"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["2026A1515010276; the 2026 Foreign Experts Program"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100003453","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["aslopubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Limnol Oceanogr Letters"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,11]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>Runoff and calved ice volumes from the Greenland Ice Sheet are well constrained, but quantifying the associated suspended sediment flux remains challenging. Here we present near\u2010terminus observations from three glacierized fjords in southeast Greenland, combining full\u2010depth turbidity profiles and current velocity from summer 2024 to evaluate sediment export. We identify extensive subsurface sediment plumes from marine\u2010terminating glaciers which are undetectable using remote sensing approaches and underrepresented in fjord sediment\u2010core reconstructions. Sediment cores document an exponential increase in sediment accumulation rates from glacier\u2010distal to glacier\u2010proximal coring sites. Therefore, the scarcity of sediment cores collected in the immediate vicinity of glacier termini suggests that sediment export from marine\u2010terminating glaciers has likely been systematically underestimated. Our findings underscore the importance of direct observations for quantifying sediment transport in glacierized fjords and suggest the Greenland Ice Sheet contributes more sediment to ocean margins than previously assumed.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/lol2.70186","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,9]],"date-time":"2026-10-09T07:09:24Z","timestamp":1791529764000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Hidden subsurface suspended sediment export from Greenland's marine\u2010terminating glaciers"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"11","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-2080-0342","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yaqing","family":"Ruan","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Marine Biogeochemistry GEOMAR Helmholtz Centre for Ocean Research Kiel  Kiel Germany"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Eric P.","family":"Achterberg","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Marine Biogeochemistry GEOMAR Helmholtz Centre for Ocean Research Kiel  Kiel Germany"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5507-3333","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Hilde","family":"Oliver","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Applied Ocean Physics and Engineering Woods Hole Oceanographic Institution  Massachusetts USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Lukas L.","family":"Taenzer","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Physical Oceanography Woods Hole Oceanographic Institution  Woods Hole Massachusetts USA"},{"name":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology  Cambridge Massachusetts USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Xin","family":"Huang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Ocean Science and Engineering Southern University of Science and Technology  Shenzhen China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Camilla S.","family":"Andresen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Glaciology and Climate Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland  Copenhagen Denmark"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Mark J.","family":"Hopwood","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Ocean Science and Engineering Southern University of Science and Technology  Shenzhen China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,9]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_2_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/s41467-024-45694-1"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/2015GL065003"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/s41467-017-00095-5"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.5194\/bg-23-1159-2026"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/s41561-018-0268-4"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.5194\/tc-6-1-2012"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_8_1","volume-title":"Glacial Marine Sedimentation; Paleoclimatic Significance","author":"Cowan E. A.","year":"1991"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_9_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/s41467-020-15579-0"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_10_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1126\/sciadv.add0610"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_11_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\